## 8. Completion Criteria

Feature engineering is complete when:

-   The forecasting target and observation frequency are unambiguous.
-   Every feature has a documented definition, unit, and availability
    time.
-   Lagged and rolling features have been checked for leakage.
-   Missing data and dropped rows are accounted for.
-   Regional features are joined at a defensible geographic level.
-   Modeling variants are exported and reproducible.
-   The same chronological evaluation window can be used to compare
    models.

## 9. Immediate Next Action

Do not begin by generating all features at once. First, inspect the
exact filenames and columns of the existing cleaned metro, weather, and
regional datasets.

Then:

1.  Confirm the schema and aggregation level of each dataset.
2.  Confirm the target variable and prediction horizon.
3.  Build and validate the hourly master dataset.
4.  Implement each feature group sequentially.
5.  Run checks after each section before proceeding.

This will avoid duplicating existing work, making incorrect joins, or
introducing leakage into the forecasting pipeline.
